WEBVTT

01:04.230 --> 01:05.982
WHEN LIFE GIVES YOU TANGERINES

01:09.694 --> 01:13.031
DAUGHTER OF YANG GWAN-SIK AND OH AE-SUN
YANG GEUM-MYEONG! ACCEPTED TO SNU!

01:20.163 --> 01:23.583
'88 SEOUL OLYMPICS CELEBRATION
ADVANCED CITIZENS! ADVANCED STREETS!

01:23.666 --> 01:27.712
So what if it's the Olympics for you?
We have the Olympics here every day too.

01:28.588 --> 01:30.799
Survival was their Olympics.

01:30.882 --> 01:33.968
No, it's not what you think.

01:34.052 --> 01:35.512
It's not like that, so…

01:35.595 --> 01:39.849
They fought through their own grand
yet cruel Olympics every single time.

01:39.933 --> 01:40.975
Please just leave!

01:41.059 --> 01:45.063
…without medals, pensions, or retirement.

01:46.356 --> 01:48.024
Why are you flipping them?

01:48.858 --> 01:52.654
What does flipping our stalls have to do
with your Olympics?

01:53.947 --> 01:58.326
Did conches and sauries protest
against the Olympics?

01:58.409 --> 01:59.661
Did they block the roads?

02:01.704 --> 02:03.748
Come on, seriously!

02:04.666 --> 02:06.376
How many times have I told you?

02:06.459 --> 02:09.129
The Olympic torch is coming through here!

02:09.212 --> 02:11.798
Americans will be watching this on TV.

02:11.881 --> 02:13.383
Should we just show them

02:13.466 --> 02:16.886
this mess of fish intestines
and a fishy stench?

02:16.970 --> 02:19.597
Do their televisions have noses
attached to them?

02:19.681 --> 02:23.143
The government has told us
to clean up things that lack aesthetics.

02:23.226 --> 02:24.727
The government!

02:24.811 --> 02:25.770
The government!

02:25.854 --> 02:27.397
Aesthetics?

02:27.897 --> 02:28.982
Aesthetics?

02:29.065 --> 02:31.693
You're taking away our livelihood

02:31.776 --> 02:34.237
to impress some people
on the other side of the world?

02:34.320 --> 02:36.948
What kind of dog crap is that?

02:37.031 --> 02:39.159
Is that how Americans do things?

02:39.242 --> 02:41.953
Taking even a beggar's bowl?

02:42.036 --> 02:42.871
For God's sake.

02:42.954 --> 02:46.166
Why don't you fight for the country
instead of selling sauries?

02:46.249 --> 02:49.377
We should accept a little loss
for the greater good.

02:49.460 --> 02:52.046
You're always nitpicking
every tiny detail!

02:52.130 --> 02:54.591
Someone greased your palm, didn't they?

02:56.259 --> 02:58.094
What, because I don't have money?

02:58.178 --> 03:01.556
How much did they pay you
for the town's blood, sweat, and tears?

03:01.639 --> 03:02.557
How much?

03:02.640 --> 03:04.642
And you call yourself our chief?

03:04.726 --> 03:07.228
Did you major in saying ten things
after hearing one?

03:07.312 --> 03:08.938
-What?
-It's next September.

03:09.022 --> 03:11.107
The torch will pass through here briefly.

03:11.191 --> 03:13.860
We live hand to mouth.
You're cutting off our source of income!

03:13.943 --> 03:15.653
What kind of law is that?

03:16.154 --> 03:17.697
What do you know about the law?

03:17.780 --> 03:19.282
Do you even know anything?

03:19.866 --> 03:21.326
Oh Ae-sun!

03:21.409 --> 03:22.869
Where is Ae-sun?

03:22.952 --> 03:26.164
Our deputy chief
is a high school graduate!

03:26.247 --> 03:27.957
She dropped out of high school.

03:28.458 --> 03:31.419
-What do you mean "graduate"?
-But she went to high school!

03:32.003 --> 03:34.380
Where is our deputy chief?

03:34.464 --> 03:37.133
-Ae-sun!
-Our deputy chief is the smartest!

03:37.217 --> 03:39.552
-Ae-sun!
-Why are you looking for her?

03:39.636 --> 03:41.930
She wouldn't know what to say!

03:42.013 --> 03:45.350
Why can't I sell my sauries
just because the nation is celebrating?

03:45.433 --> 03:47.727
Why do your sauries even matter now?

03:48.353 --> 03:50.396
If North Korea wants to ruin the Olympics

03:50.480 --> 03:53.274
and open the Mount Kumgang dam,
all of Seoul will be flooded.

03:53.358 --> 03:56.027
They say that even the 63 SQUARE
will be submerged.

03:56.110 --> 03:59.113
Do you keep up with current affairs?
Do you understand the greater good?

03:59.197 --> 04:03.743
Are sauries really more important
than the great…ness of history?

04:03.826 --> 04:05.578
Of course they're important!

04:05.662 --> 04:07.622
-They're important!
-So frustrating.

04:10.458 --> 04:12.710
You think a rebellion happens
for no reason?

04:12.794 --> 04:17.924
Even a dog will crap all over and leave
if you tip over its food bowl!

04:18.007 --> 04:19.717
Do you want some of ours?

04:19.801 --> 04:21.636
-Let go!
-Do you want some?

04:22.428 --> 04:24.555
Ae-sun!

04:25.556 --> 04:28.059
She's here. Here's Ae-sun.

04:28.142 --> 04:29.143
There you are.

04:30.019 --> 04:30.853
Hey!

04:32.105 --> 04:33.690
Hey. Deputy.

04:35.650 --> 04:36.567
Hey! Deputy!

04:50.915 --> 04:53.501
Is she the crap you mentioned? Is she?

04:58.006 --> 04:59.299
You better get up.

05:00.508 --> 05:02.385
This is a silent outcry…

05:03.261 --> 05:04.470
What did you say?

05:04.554 --> 05:07.265
Lashed by the scourge
Of the bitter season…

05:07.348 --> 05:10.268
If you're embarrassed, just get up.
Don't try anything.

05:11.436 --> 05:13.146
If you choose to leave…

05:13.229 --> 05:14.188
Hey, call a forklift!

05:14.272 --> 05:15.398
Let it roll over me!

05:15.481 --> 05:18.151
Hey, this is a gangster,
not a high school graduate.

05:18.234 --> 05:21.821
Taking people's livelihoods away
makes you a gangster, not me.

05:21.904 --> 05:23.781
What did you just say?

05:23.865 --> 05:24.824
Roll over me.

05:24.907 --> 05:27.035
Seriously, what's wrong with you?

05:27.118 --> 05:28.411
Roll over me!

05:28.494 --> 05:30.663
Just do as you're told!

05:30.747 --> 05:32.540
I said roll over me!

05:34.459 --> 05:36.002
Roll over me!

05:42.675 --> 05:45.470
Hey, what happened to our Literary Girl?

05:46.596 --> 05:47.638
What do you mean?

05:48.222 --> 05:49.891
Life happened, that's what.

05:49.974 --> 05:51.225
Goddamn it!

05:52.852 --> 05:54.395
For goodness' sake!

05:54.479 --> 05:55.688
Hey, Bu Sang-gil!

05:55.772 --> 05:58.775
You betrayed the people's trust,
and you'll definitely pay the price.

06:01.319 --> 06:03.363
Politics is like the wind, you know?

06:03.446 --> 06:05.239
Rumors are spreading like wildfire

06:05.323 --> 06:07.575
that Ae-sun will be
the next fishing co-op chief.

06:07.658 --> 06:10.578
Come on, I have no interest in politics.

06:10.661 --> 06:11.913
I think you'll run for office.

06:11.996 --> 06:14.624
People like her always end up
running for office.

06:15.708 --> 06:18.753
This election will be
between a stooge and a freedom fighter.

06:18.836 --> 06:21.339
That spineless traitor.

06:21.422 --> 06:23.549
If we side with that treacherous stooge,

06:23.633 --> 06:26.052
they'll screw us over
right under our noses.

06:26.135 --> 06:28.429
So what if he's the chief.

06:28.513 --> 06:30.723
How dare he call a person "deputy"!

06:30.807 --> 06:33.976
Deputy Chief is the official title,
and he's always like, "Deputy!"

06:34.060 --> 06:36.104
"Hey, Deputy!" That's how he addresses me.

06:36.187 --> 06:38.189
She never liked being a deputy.

06:38.272 --> 06:40.316
If a dog can be the chief, why can't you?

06:40.400 --> 06:43.277
Let's make a chief
out of one of our haenyeo crew.

06:43.361 --> 06:47.281
I really have no interest in politics!

06:47.365 --> 06:51.619
You won't let your darling
Gwan-sik's dream come true?

06:53.955 --> 06:55.665
What's gotten into you?

06:56.749 --> 07:00.002
Our captain must be
campaigning for someone.

07:00.753 --> 07:01.838
What's this for?

07:01.921 --> 07:03.756
Who do you want us to vote for?

07:04.674 --> 07:07.301
Captain Yang,
now that you've paid me off, speak up.

07:07.844 --> 07:08.678
Well…

07:10.263 --> 07:12.390
I'm not saying this because she's my wife.

07:12.932 --> 07:16.185
But Ae-sun was class president
back in the day.

07:16.269 --> 07:17.478
I saw it myself.

07:19.605 --> 07:21.065
I can honestly say

07:21.149 --> 07:25.153
that I've never met anyone
as smart as Ae-sun.

07:25.236 --> 07:27.822
Have you ever been smart enough
to become class president?

07:37.081 --> 07:38.583
Let's be frank between us.

07:38.666 --> 07:41.878
Do you actually want Ae-sun
to be the chief?

07:42.837 --> 07:46.507
Your wife would be
the first female chief of Dodong-ri.

07:46.591 --> 07:48.092
What does that make you?

07:48.176 --> 07:51.387
A real man should have some pride.

07:51.971 --> 07:54.182
Yes, she'd be the first, but so would I.

07:54.265 --> 07:56.767
If Ae-sun becomes the first female chief,

07:57.268 --> 07:59.729
I'd be the first husband of a chief.

08:00.730 --> 08:03.483
Pride is even better
when you earn it without effort.

08:03.983 --> 08:05.985
That's enough, okay?

08:06.068 --> 08:08.279
You're making the rest of us men
look like trash.

08:08.362 --> 08:11.199
Our captain has dreams
that are very different from ours.

08:13.743 --> 08:16.662
So, this is a brand-new item.

08:20.166 --> 08:23.711
I'm going to do all of it.
I'll be the chief of the fishing co-op.

08:23.794 --> 08:26.005
I'm also going to be
the president five times.

08:29.300 --> 08:30.676
What do you want to become?

08:30.760 --> 08:32.512
Don't even ask him!

08:34.639 --> 08:35.765
The First Lady.

08:37.808 --> 08:38.768
The First Lady.

08:39.727 --> 08:40.895
So…

08:40.978 --> 08:42.813
What is it? First Lady.

08:43.523 --> 08:46.984
I think they put… real bananas in those.

08:47.068 --> 08:48.653
Premium bananas.

08:51.531 --> 08:52.490
You drank it all.

08:55.368 --> 08:56.202
Hey, man.

08:56.285 --> 08:58.246
This banana milk is nothing.

08:58.329 --> 09:01.290
That tightwad is buying pork for everyone.

09:01.374 --> 09:03.251
Who in the world doesn't like pork?

09:03.334 --> 09:04.335
SALT-GRILLED PORK

09:04.418 --> 09:05.836
Not just any pig.

09:06.420 --> 09:07.880
Jeju Black pig, you know?

09:08.548 --> 09:09.549
Jeju Black pig.

09:10.132 --> 09:11.926
Premium Jeju Black pig.

09:12.009 --> 09:14.804
Give each table an extra portion
that looks like a double.

09:14.887 --> 09:16.806
We only serve Jeju Black pig.

09:17.515 --> 09:20.810
I really don't have any ulterior motive.

09:20.893 --> 09:23.896
Look, I have no shortage
of money or honor.

09:24.605 --> 09:27.316
I only ever have one concern on my mind.

09:27.900 --> 09:31.237
How can I give our co-op members
one more thing to eat?

09:31.320 --> 09:34.991
"How can I find one more thing to give?"

09:37.285 --> 09:40.746
Listen, you should pay attention
while you eat.

09:41.289 --> 09:45.585
You squeeze all of us into this tiny place
just so we can nibble on the pork.

09:46.711 --> 09:49.422
Finish your plate,
then you can order more.

09:50.298 --> 09:52.758
I don't think you'd vote for me,
but you're here.

09:52.842 --> 09:56.429
You should bribe generously.
What a stingy briber.

09:57.388 --> 09:59.098
So, anyway,

10:00.141 --> 10:02.727
Oh Ae-sun appeared out of nowhere,

10:02.810 --> 10:04.979
but I hail from Dodong-ri.

10:05.062 --> 10:07.607
I am the rightful heir to the--

10:07.690 --> 10:10.943
I asked for a soda ages ago.

10:11.027 --> 10:13.112
Not everyone can hold a big title, right?

10:13.613 --> 10:16.449
We need to carefully examine
the candidates' backgrounds

10:16.532 --> 10:19.535
and any family issues they may have.

10:19.619 --> 10:21.829
What problems does the deputy chief have?

10:21.912 --> 10:24.957
Gwan-sik is receiving a commendation.
Do you have one?

10:25.041 --> 10:27.710
It's a plaque of appreciation,
not a commendation.

10:27.793 --> 10:30.171
I could easily get
more than a dozen of those.

10:30.796 --> 10:32.506
-You know--
-But you don't have any.

10:32.590 --> 10:34.508
Have you ever saved anyone from drowning?

10:34.592 --> 10:36.927
Stop cutting me off already!

10:37.011 --> 10:39.221
Learn to listen when others are talking.

10:39.305 --> 10:42.516
These women talk about what they want
every chance they get.

10:42.600 --> 10:45.728
How about you? Why act like
you didn't hear me ask for a soda?

10:46.729 --> 10:48.105
As you all know,

10:48.189 --> 10:51.275
that family isn't exactly
a great example for others.

10:52.109 --> 10:56.614
They ran away from home at 18
and had a daughter.

10:57.198 --> 10:58.908
She's a student at SNU.

10:58.991 --> 11:00.618
Not their second child.

11:01.744 --> 11:05.539
There's no need to talk about
someone else's kid, but…

11:07.041 --> 11:08.167
Never mind. I shouldn't.

11:08.250 --> 11:10.711
Then don't. And get me a soda!

11:10.795 --> 11:13.547
If you sow beans, you'll only reap beans.

11:13.631 --> 11:17.593
Being a nutjob is hereditary, you know?

11:21.597 --> 11:25.184
DODONG-RI FISHING CO-OP DEPUTY CHIEF
MOTHER OF YANG EUN-MYEONG

11:25.267 --> 11:26.936
DODONG-RI FISHING CO-OP CHIEF

11:35.361 --> 11:37.154
Wait, have you been to the salon?

11:41.325 --> 11:42.410
Take this off.

11:44.036 --> 11:46.831
How many student leaders' moms are coming?

11:46.914 --> 11:47.832
All of them?

11:50.584 --> 11:52.753
But wait, you were the PE leader?

11:53.546 --> 11:54.505
Why you?

11:55.089 --> 11:56.590
That's funny.

11:59.301 --> 12:03.973
The other moms are gonna flip out
when they get here,

12:04.056 --> 12:06.851
asking how your sister
got into Seoul National University

12:06.934 --> 12:09.770
and what the secret was. Goodness me.

12:10.271 --> 12:11.355
Someone's excited.

12:12.815 --> 12:14.608
It's at 4:00, right? Let's go.

12:15.651 --> 12:17.945
-Mom.
-Am I a bit early?

12:18.946 --> 12:21.323
-Mother!
-Should I go to the faculty room?

12:21.407 --> 12:22.867
There aren't any other moms.

12:24.118 --> 12:27.455
Why not? You said they invited
all the leaders' mothers to come.

12:27.955 --> 12:29.039
It's just you.

12:29.123 --> 12:30.207
Why?

12:33.627 --> 12:35.463
Hello, sir.

12:35.546 --> 12:37.715
No need to come in. Let's go out.

12:37.798 --> 12:38.632
Pardon me?

12:39.842 --> 12:40.760
Let's go outside.

12:51.562 --> 12:53.939
My car is now an Onata?

12:56.525 --> 13:00.112
The Chinese teacher's car is now Pon!

13:00.196 --> 13:02.698
Our dear Eun-myeong
is getting all the kids into university.

13:02.782 --> 13:05.576
So that's it, huh? Anyone gets in
if you get them the initials?

13:05.659 --> 13:07.161
Is that how your sister got in?

13:07.745 --> 13:11.540
He doesn't just give them away.
He takes them off and sells them.

13:13.584 --> 13:16.837
Ma'am, this is a very serious matter.

13:16.921 --> 13:21.467
The principal's car is now a Tellar!

13:23.260 --> 13:25.805
I've been teaching for about 20 years.

13:25.888 --> 13:30.476
Yang Eun-myeong is the first to ever turn
a teacher's car into an Onata!

13:31.060 --> 13:32.228
I'm sorry.

13:32.311 --> 13:34.230
Your son seems like he's here to work.

13:34.730 --> 13:36.357
I heard he's good with his hands.

13:37.525 --> 13:40.820
He cuts a set of ten bus tickets
into eleven

13:40.903 --> 13:42.488
and makes a profit of 50 won.

13:42.571 --> 13:46.283
The coin game's being played out there?
That'll be Eun-myeong, then!

13:47.284 --> 13:50.287
Is school some kind of gambling den?
Is he running a business here?

13:50.788 --> 13:52.331
Is he a teacher or something?

13:53.332 --> 13:56.252
Why would a student come to school
to earn a paycheck?

13:57.378 --> 13:58.212
I'm sorry.

13:58.295 --> 14:01.549
Did you give your daughter your all
but go hands-off with your son?

14:02.800 --> 14:05.594
Do you know what kind of kids
your son hangs out with?

14:20.276 --> 14:21.443
Keep your distance.

14:23.487 --> 14:24.822
Don't even talk to me.

14:27.908 --> 14:30.786
You said it was just a leaders' meeting!

14:31.829 --> 14:33.539
Who told you to make money?

14:34.039 --> 14:35.916
Why don't you study? Why focus on money?

14:36.000 --> 14:37.918
I never felt embarrassed

14:38.002 --> 14:40.462
coming to school for your sister.

14:40.546 --> 14:43.632
But now, I can't hold my head up!

14:44.633 --> 14:45.801
Stop hitting that!

14:50.014 --> 14:52.808
What's wrong with you?
What did I ever do to you?

14:52.892 --> 14:55.394
I told you to do half
of what your sister did, didn't I?

14:55.477 --> 14:57.062
I raised both of you the same way.

14:57.146 --> 14:59.189
Do half as well
so you can become the chief?

14:59.273 --> 15:01.901
Being a nutjob is in the genes,
so I'll be in your way.

15:01.984 --> 15:04.445
Don't listen to what people say!

15:04.528 --> 15:07.364
-I hate Bu Sang-gil.
-You're embarrassed by me, aren't you?

15:08.407 --> 15:10.409
You only want to be
Geum-myeong's mom, huh?

15:33.766 --> 15:36.936
Not everyone in her family is a nutjob.

15:37.019 --> 15:39.563
But education isn't everything in life.

15:39.647 --> 15:41.649
Whose daughter is she, after all?

15:43.651 --> 15:45.819
Sure, she's up in Seoul,

15:46.820 --> 15:49.907
but she's just going to end up
a dating queen too.

15:49.990 --> 15:51.784
CELEBRATING DIRECT PRESIDENTIAL
ELECTION SYSTEM

15:59.041 --> 16:01.919
He always picks her up these days.
Is that her boyfriend?

16:02.002 --> 16:03.337
Is he rich or something?

16:03.837 --> 16:06.423
Even if he is, how can a college student
drive a car like that?

16:07.132 --> 16:08.801
Something's off about that girl.

16:09.927 --> 16:13.055
Look at the news.
Lots of college girls work as escorts.

16:13.138 --> 16:16.225
They get paid to go on dates
and spend time with older men.

16:17.434 --> 16:18.268
Ju-gyeong.

16:19.144 --> 16:20.229
Show some respect.

16:32.825 --> 16:34.159
Is he from the US?

16:35.327 --> 16:38.539
Is he not embarrassed?
He's opening the door for her in public.

16:38.622 --> 16:41.333
Guys like that cut pork cutlets
for girls at restaurants.

17:09.028 --> 17:14.199
Love is all I know

17:20.372 --> 17:21.957
Whose child is she?

17:22.041 --> 17:27.046
As they say, it's so blindingly obvious.
I don't even need eyes to see it.

17:28.213 --> 17:32.968
That family never cared
about keeping boys and girls apart.

17:34.386 --> 17:38.557
Hey, you may have bought the tree,
but that rock isn't yours, is it?

17:38.640 --> 17:41.018
Why did you write your name
on the public property?

17:41.101 --> 17:42.061
Think about it.

17:42.978 --> 17:45.564
She should be grateful
to be the deputy chief,

17:45.647 --> 17:46.690
but she has no clue.

17:46.774 --> 17:48.233
Who does she think she is?

17:48.317 --> 17:49.151
Hey, Captain.

17:49.234 --> 17:51.487
Do you actually have any campaign pledges?

17:51.570 --> 17:52.571
What?

17:52.654 --> 17:55.157
I think you're splashing out
just to bash your opponent.

17:58.368 --> 18:00.287
I'm not bashing anyone.

18:00.370 --> 18:02.081
I'm just discussing morality.

18:02.164 --> 18:04.583
Don't you realize
people have the right to know?

18:04.666 --> 18:05.584
Don't you know?

18:05.667 --> 18:06.627
BADA SEAFOOD HOUSE

18:07.377 --> 18:09.630
Why would he bring your kids into this?

18:10.923 --> 18:13.884
Shit-gil crossed the line with that one.

18:14.885 --> 18:16.095
You fight back too.

18:17.179 --> 18:20.349
If you keep this up,
Ae-sun's going to fight back.

18:20.432 --> 18:23.268
Ae-sun's just holding back
because she has class.

18:23.352 --> 18:25.479
If she really wanted to play dirty,

18:25.562 --> 18:28.232
you wouldn't exactly come out
looking so clean either.

18:28.732 --> 18:32.653
Sang-gil's father was the first
during the Japanese occupation.

18:33.278 --> 18:36.240
First to surrender his Korean name
to the Japanese in Jeju.

18:38.700 --> 18:40.077
Hold on.

18:40.160 --> 18:43.330
There's nothing you can say about me,
even if you want to.

18:43.413 --> 18:44.790
I'm a man

18:46.041 --> 18:48.585
who makes donations to our government.

18:49.169 --> 18:50.295
As for Oh Ae-sun?

18:50.379 --> 18:54.508
I'm pretty sure
she's never given a dime to charity.

18:56.802 --> 18:59.638
Politics is just a field
of dog crap anyway.

18:59.721 --> 19:02.641
If you're going to roll in it,
black fur is better than white.

19:02.724 --> 19:05.477
Who cares what fur a dog has
if it rolls around in crap?

19:05.561 --> 19:07.104
It's just a dog with crap on it.

19:07.187 --> 19:09.273
I'm going to win with my pledges.

19:10.149 --> 19:13.902
Wow, Oh Ae-sun is still so noble.

19:13.986 --> 19:16.822
You're not handing out soap.
You're not feeding them pork.

19:16.905 --> 19:18.907
And you're not playing dirty?

19:18.991 --> 19:20.993
Then you're going to lose.

19:22.202 --> 19:27.624
Ae-sun, the co-op members have the right
to know Sang-gil's true colors.

19:27.708 --> 19:30.210
He was the first to cross the line.

19:30.294 --> 19:32.462
You might as well too.

19:32.546 --> 19:36.967
A cocoon that doesn't break open in time
gets devoured by predators.

19:37.050 --> 19:41.597
Only the ones that break free quickly
emerge as butterflies.

19:41.680 --> 19:45.976
You need to learn how to open the doors
that are in your way, just like this.

19:46.852 --> 19:49.313
In every ferry
That reaches the Oryukdo Islets

19:51.106 --> 19:55.903
People can take turns to bad-mouth me

19:55.986 --> 19:58.989
No matter how hard they try

20:00.073 --> 20:05.204
They won't find a speck of dust on me

20:05.829 --> 20:08.999
That's the worst thing about me

20:09.583 --> 20:13.921
Try to find something on me all you want

20:14.004 --> 20:15.047
Stop singing!

20:15.130 --> 20:17.507
I'm not voting for you
if I lose my appetite.

20:18.383 --> 20:20.093
Damn it!

20:20.177 --> 20:21.720
Hey, where are my noodles?

20:24.097 --> 20:25.724
He's always picking on his wife.

20:27.601 --> 20:30.771
You can't even make noodles quickly.

20:31.939 --> 20:33.065
Just walk home.

20:33.649 --> 20:35.651
Don't get in my car. Got it?

20:35.734 --> 20:36.944
Hey, Bu Sang-gil.

20:37.694 --> 20:40.155
Your surname means "deputy" anyway.

20:40.239 --> 20:42.699
It means you're the "deputy" captain
on the boat

20:42.783 --> 20:44.993
and the "deputy" chief
for the fishing co-op.

20:48.038 --> 20:50.040
-Hey!
-Are you voting for me or not?

20:50.123 --> 20:54.002
Why do you always come and pick a fight?
Is it because I didn't buy you a soda?

20:54.086 --> 20:57.130
Hey, in case you lose the election…

20:57.214 --> 20:58.382
Why would I lose?

20:58.465 --> 21:01.426
Do you know how much the pork
and noodles cost?

21:01.927 --> 21:04.388
Just be content
with being the deputy chief.

21:04.471 --> 21:06.515
Even on the Animal Quiz Show,

21:06.598 --> 21:08.725
if the Alpha is defeated,

21:09.226 --> 21:13.855
it will instantly become the pack Omega.

21:13.939 --> 21:15.565
-Hey!
-"Hey"?

21:15.649 --> 21:16.900
Did you say "hey"?

21:16.984 --> 21:19.444
-"Hey"?
-Am I getting those noodles anytime today?

21:21.613 --> 21:23.615
You can vote for Oh Ae-sun if you want.

21:24.992 --> 21:26.785
FROM BU SANG-GIL, CANDIDATE 1

21:26.868 --> 21:30.247
The Oh may be smart,
and the Bu may be lacking,

21:31.123 --> 21:32.416
but a female chief?

21:32.499 --> 21:33.875
Nowhere in this nation!

21:33.959 --> 21:36.628
-No, of course not.
-A box of cigarettes each.

21:37.754 --> 21:39.881
I wish it was always election season.

21:40.924 --> 21:43.552
How can a gentle breeze
from the pines stop a typhoon?

21:44.052 --> 21:46.555
Democracy? It's all about numbers.

21:47.055 --> 21:48.682
Stick with the majority.

21:49.349 --> 21:51.351
The chief must be the Bu!

21:54.229 --> 21:55.063
All right!

21:55.147 --> 21:55.981
Pour me some.

21:56.940 --> 21:57.774
Now!

21:59.318 --> 22:01.278
-The chief is…
-The Bu!

22:02.154 --> 22:04.364
-The chief is…
-The Bu!

22:04.448 --> 22:07.993
-The chief is…
-The Bu!

22:11.455 --> 22:12.706
Lucky you.

22:12.789 --> 22:14.333
I hope you're the chief forever.

22:14.958 --> 22:19.296
Indecency runs in that family!

22:19.379 --> 22:20.672
I named my daughters

22:20.756 --> 22:23.008
Hyeon-suk for "virtuous"
and Jeong-suk for "pure."

22:23.091 --> 22:23.925
And I

22:24.885 --> 22:26.970
like those who are virtuous.

22:27.679 --> 22:29.181
What a load of crap.

22:37.481 --> 22:38.357
I am

22:39.983 --> 22:43.403
a candidate with nothing to be ashamed of.

22:45.280 --> 22:46.490
The thing is,

22:47.199 --> 22:50.786
life has been so difficult for me.

22:51.536 --> 22:56.249
We could clear out all the street stalls,
and I still wouldn't make much from it.

22:58.335 --> 23:02.172
A real estate office in this small town
barely makes any money.

23:02.255 --> 23:06.927
I just wanted to make a little dough
from the Olympics,

23:07.010 --> 23:09.429
but those haenyeo are so stubborn.

23:10.847 --> 23:12.057
For real, you know me.

23:12.641 --> 23:14.393
-Yeah.
-I'm a softie.

23:14.893 --> 23:16.269
Mi-suk, you know me.

23:17.312 --> 23:18.688
I'll take care of everything.

23:19.189 --> 23:20.148
Without a doubt,

23:21.024 --> 23:24.027
I'm going to be the chief again.

23:25.237 --> 23:26.071
Really?

23:26.571 --> 23:29.324
You'd really take care of everything?

23:29.408 --> 23:31.785
I don't need to pay you a fee or anything?

23:31.868 --> 23:32.911
Just give me 30.

23:33.912 --> 23:35.831
-What?
-You keep 70%. I'll take 30.

23:38.667 --> 23:40.252
Right, I see.

23:41.086 --> 23:43.505
Even a flea's liver should be shared.

23:43.588 --> 23:49.177
Mi-suk, I'm Bu Sang-gil of Dodong-ri.

23:49.886 --> 23:50.762
Mi-suk.

23:51.847 --> 23:56.476
I don't have romance in my life,
but I do have money.

23:56.560 --> 23:57.394
I am

23:58.728 --> 24:00.647
just one lonely man.

24:04.776 --> 24:06.653
There's no need to be shy around me.

24:09.281 --> 24:10.323
I'm not shy.

24:12.159 --> 24:14.077
No, I mean…

24:14.870 --> 24:18.707
You think I'd help you
do all this for money?

24:19.624 --> 24:22.836
Then what are you doing it for?

24:26.590 --> 24:27.799
What are you looking at?

24:29.718 --> 24:31.595
Come on.

24:32.804 --> 24:34.806
It's the Olympics, right?

24:35.390 --> 24:37.809
Even the Soviet Union
chose to stand hand in hand

24:37.893 --> 24:40.687
and break down the walls.

24:41.396 --> 24:42.814
Why don't we break down…

24:44.900 --> 24:46.151
the wall between us?

24:52.032 --> 24:54.910
Eat this. Your stomach will hurt.

24:54.993 --> 24:55.827
Wait.

24:55.911 --> 25:00.248
Mi-suk's saury just struck me
like an arrow in the heart.

25:03.877 --> 25:06.087
Perhaps this isn't just any saury.

25:06.171 --> 25:09.758
Is it okay to think of it
as Mi-suk's heart instead?

25:11.426 --> 25:12.677
Yeah, sure.

25:13.512 --> 25:14.429
Abalone?

25:15.222 --> 25:19.392
You make everything else in the world
seem like baloney.

25:23.396 --> 25:25.065
Just eat the shrimp.

25:26.858 --> 25:30.946
Now you mention it,
you're making my shrimp…

25:31.738 --> 25:32.739
You're so silly!

25:32.822 --> 25:33.949
What? What's wrong?

25:34.032 --> 25:35.659
You're making me really excited.

25:36.201 --> 25:38.370
You make my heart excited. What?

25:38.954 --> 25:40.914
You're witty. I'll give you that.

25:47.921 --> 25:48.880
Hey, you…

25:51.341 --> 25:53.343
came here to eat some sea squirts.

25:54.719 --> 25:57.055
Why are you serenading my solitude?

26:00.892 --> 26:01.726
That tickles.

26:04.813 --> 26:05.814
Disgusting.

26:06.565 --> 26:09.276
You're so disgusting. Seriously.

26:10.193 --> 26:14.864
You need to learn how to open the doors
that are in your way, just like this.

26:18.034 --> 26:19.369
Wait. What's all this…

26:20.287 --> 26:23.123
What are you doing here? Damn it.

26:24.332 --> 26:27.043
I was wondering
why you chose to be the stooge.

26:27.711 --> 26:31.131
You're so disgusting
that we can't even crack open sea squirts.

26:31.631 --> 26:33.800
What the hell are you doing here again?

26:33.883 --> 26:38.138
Who do you think you are,
meddling in my life all the time?

26:38.221 --> 26:41.099
This is my part-time job. So what?

26:41.933 --> 26:45.228
While a saury struck your heart,

26:45.312 --> 26:47.939
she was cracking open another sea squirt.

26:48.023 --> 26:50.900
Wait, why were you eavesdropping on us?

26:50.984 --> 26:51.985
-Why?
-Hey!

26:53.570 --> 26:56.990
You just want to be chief so you can
massage another woman's feet, huh?

26:59.659 --> 27:00.577
Goddamn it!

27:01.453 --> 27:04.247
But you can't even be the chief anymore.

27:09.794 --> 27:11.004
Why can't I be?

27:11.087 --> 27:12.088
Why?

27:12.172 --> 27:16.343
A stray dog runs around the neighborhood
causing all kinds of trouble.

27:16.426 --> 27:19.638
You're just a mutt
trying to hump every woman's leg.

27:19.721 --> 27:20.889
Hey!

27:20.972 --> 27:24.184
We wouldn't even give
a mutt like you rotten rice.

27:24.684 --> 27:28.313
But you still want to be chief?
Stop crapping all over town!

27:31.274 --> 27:32.233
Goddamn it!

27:33.068 --> 27:36.404
Hey, come on.
Do you even know what happened?

27:36.946 --> 27:38.531
What do you know?

27:38.615 --> 27:43.286
She said she was just getting cramps
in her toes, so--

27:43.370 --> 27:46.164
Well, your wife's getting cramps
in her heart.

27:47.082 --> 27:48.124
"A great example"?

27:48.208 --> 27:50.960
The candidate's "family problems,"
you say?

27:51.044 --> 27:53.171
It's better for a candidate's son
to be a nutjob

27:53.254 --> 27:54.839
than for a candidate to be.

27:55.799 --> 27:57.550
He's actually pretty clever!

27:57.634 --> 28:02.472
So what now?
Are you going to tell people about me?

28:02.555 --> 28:04.891
Of course we are.

28:04.974 --> 28:07.519
We are going to
so that Ae-sun can be chief.

28:07.602 --> 28:08.561
That's right.

28:08.645 --> 28:11.856
Hey, you. Is that what you stand for?

28:13.149 --> 28:14.442
"Right to know."

28:15.360 --> 28:16.319
"Morality."

28:16.903 --> 28:19.114
I'm not bashing anyone.

28:19.197 --> 28:20.949
I'm just discussing morality.

28:21.533 --> 28:23.702
Don't you realize
people have the right to know?

28:23.785 --> 28:25.453
Isn't that what you like?

28:25.537 --> 28:28.206
Wow, Ae-sun.

28:30.125 --> 28:30.959
Goddamn it!

28:37.882 --> 28:39.300
This is so silly.

28:39.384 --> 28:42.011
CONGRATULATIONS
THE 7TH DODONG-RI CHIEF, OH AE-SUN

28:42.095 --> 28:45.807
Oh Ae-sun!

28:47.100 --> 28:48.935
The small ball that Ae-sun launched…

28:49.018 --> 28:51.396
Goodness me. Look at this!

28:51.479 --> 28:52.814
Did the school lend this to us?

28:52.897 --> 28:55.233
They only use it once a year
for sports day.

28:55.984 --> 28:58.945
…came back down, bursting open in half.

28:59.028 --> 29:00.447
And Jeju had…

29:00.530 --> 29:01.364
Chief!

29:01.448 --> 29:02.574
…its first-ever female chief.

29:02.657 --> 29:05.493
Chief! Chief Oh!

29:06.119 --> 29:07.245
Yes!

29:07.328 --> 29:09.122
-The rice cake is here.
-It's here now?

29:09.914 --> 29:13.209
-Chief Oh, we're out of makgeolli.
-Really?

29:14.169 --> 29:15.128
Chief Oh.

29:15.211 --> 29:16.504
Can I have a blanket?

29:16.588 --> 29:17.797
Yes.

29:17.881 --> 29:22.177
Chief! The school wants to know
when you'll return the confetti ball.

29:23.845 --> 29:26.222
It must have pulled at her heartstrings.

29:30.101 --> 29:33.062
Many years later,
Mom joined Lim Young-woong's fan club,

29:33.772 --> 29:36.691
and her username was "Chief Oh."

29:39.861 --> 29:40.695
Chief!

29:40.779 --> 29:45.074
Chief, come over here
and have a taste. Come on!

29:45.158 --> 29:46.075
Coming!

29:46.826 --> 29:48.036
I'm coming!

29:58.129 --> 29:59.547
-Go ahead and take that.
-Okay.

30:07.263 --> 30:09.682
THE 5TH AND 6TH FISHING CO-OP CHIEF
BU SANG-GIL

30:22.987 --> 30:24.572
Are we ever getting any meat?

30:25.073 --> 30:26.908
Are you saving it up or something?

30:26.991 --> 30:30.829
Why would you come all the way
just to be grumpy?

30:30.912 --> 30:33.623
A predecessor would never miss
an inauguration ceremony.

30:33.706 --> 30:37.585
I'm the former king who's here to check
on a nobody who knows jack shit.

30:38.711 --> 30:41.005
You came because you'd look petty
if you didn't.

30:41.631 --> 30:43.842
I've resigned.

30:44.676 --> 30:46.177
I stepped down myself.

30:47.095 --> 30:50.849
You know the 80-year-old grandpa
who owns the variety shop?

30:52.350 --> 30:54.811
He hardly ever says anything,

30:55.436 --> 30:59.315
but he asked if I knew about Sang-gil
massaging the real estate agent's feet.

31:00.316 --> 31:04.529
Come on! She had toe cramps!

31:05.488 --> 31:07.407
I had to save the person first!

31:20.753 --> 31:23.673
Looks like I'll have to serve
my chief daughter-in-law for life.

31:24.173 --> 31:27.343
Thanks to her meddling,
the family's full of officials.

31:27.427 --> 31:30.179
If she's the chief,
Gwan-sik's like a king consort.

31:30.889 --> 31:32.765
That'd make me the queen mother, right?

31:32.849 --> 31:36.102
My goodness, she is making a fuss again.

31:36.185 --> 31:40.231
She's something else.
Her luck changed after meeting Gwan-sik.

31:40.315 --> 31:42.775
You're bragging, aren't you?

31:43.860 --> 31:44.777
Bragging?

31:45.778 --> 31:48.364
On that note,
I hear your daughter-in-law plays cards.

31:49.032 --> 31:50.325
Hey, that's…

31:50.408 --> 31:52.994
Isn't the pajeon ready yet?

31:53.077 --> 31:55.371
Our First Lady sure is busy.

31:55.455 --> 31:57.081
Don't call him the First Lady.

31:58.750 --> 32:01.419
Hey, why can't you take that apron off?

32:01.502 --> 32:02.754
-Mom.
-What?

32:02.837 --> 32:04.631
Make them bigger.

32:06.257 --> 32:07.175
Damn it.

32:08.843 --> 32:10.887
He's really pissing me off.

32:12.305 --> 32:16.935
You like that your daughter-in-law
is the chief, but you also don't like it.

32:17.435 --> 32:18.770
What's so funny?

32:19.562 --> 32:21.230
I don't think I've seen you before.

32:21.314 --> 32:22.398
-You know me?
-Chief Oh.

32:22.482 --> 32:24.025
Yes, I'm coming!

32:24.108 --> 32:25.485
Chief Oh is on her way!

32:30.531 --> 32:32.617
-Oh my!
-Why are you so surprised?

32:32.700 --> 32:35.161
Like you've never made me
work for you before?

32:35.244 --> 32:38.247
Is this revenge?
You're taking your revenge on me, right?

32:38.873 --> 32:41.084
Isn't there any respect around here?

32:41.167 --> 32:42.001
Unbelievable.

32:42.085 --> 32:45.588
How could you let the wife
of my predecessor make jeon here?

32:49.884 --> 32:53.554
I'm telling you,
Bu Sang-gil was massaging her feet!

32:57.141 --> 33:00.979
As you know, during election campaigns,

33:01.771 --> 33:03.982
people bring up all sorts of things,

33:04.065 --> 33:07.652
like how someone's great-grandfather
used to have a mistress and all that.

33:08.152 --> 33:10.446
Like how I used to go dancing?

33:10.530 --> 33:12.198
You never brought that up.

33:14.742 --> 33:20.081
It wasn't my intention, but I feel like
I've caused a stir in your household.

33:21.207 --> 33:26.838
But we took care of
the real estate woman ourselves.

33:27.463 --> 33:28.840
I couldn't care less.

33:29.340 --> 33:32.802
Gyeong-suk from the salon
and Mi-suk from the real estate office.

33:33.469 --> 33:34.971
On this tiny island,

33:35.054 --> 33:38.057
there are so many women
with such poor taste in men.

33:39.308 --> 33:44.313
Well, I guess the worst of them
is me, Park Yeong-ran.

33:48.234 --> 33:50.361
Anyway, you should go.

33:50.445 --> 33:53.197
Some people just gossip
for no good reason.

33:53.281 --> 33:55.575
Do you think they'll say
I have no dignity?

33:56.451 --> 34:02.373
No, but I feel kind of sorry
that you're making jeon for us.

34:02.457 --> 34:05.251
I have a reason to be here.

34:05.960 --> 34:07.670
I have every right to be here.

34:09.714 --> 34:11.049
I voted for you,

34:12.967 --> 34:17.638
so I think I should be able to enjoy
a drink you provide.

34:21.392 --> 34:22.393
Yeong-ran.

34:23.811 --> 34:27.356
When you go home,
no, for the rest of your life,

34:27.940 --> 34:30.318
tell your husband
that you voted for him, okay?

34:31.944 --> 34:33.613
Hey, Park Yeong-ran!

34:33.696 --> 34:35.406
I'm asking who you voted for!

34:45.625 --> 34:48.920
Why can't you answer me?
You didn't vote for me, did you?

34:49.003 --> 34:51.255
Is Mom the easiest target in the world?

34:51.839 --> 34:53.341
Hey, you little brat.

34:53.424 --> 34:55.468
Are you disrespecting me?
What do you know?

34:56.052 --> 34:58.554
You don't even know a damn thing.

35:03.059 --> 35:03.893
Why?

35:04.685 --> 35:06.771
Why?

35:07.313 --> 35:09.690
Why did the governor attend?

35:09.774 --> 35:13.236
Why did he come
to the co-op chief's inauguration?

35:13.319 --> 35:14.779
He didn't come to mine.

35:14.862 --> 35:16.114
The governor came?

35:16.197 --> 35:20.993
It was the governor who presented Gwan-sik
with the plaque of appreciation.

35:21.077 --> 35:22.662
A person who jumped into the water?

35:23.246 --> 35:26.833
If I saw them,
I would save them countless times too.

35:26.916 --> 35:29.210
I'd receive a commendation!

35:29.293 --> 35:33.464
That thing about the reward?
And he's sending them on a trip too?

35:34.423 --> 35:37.844
The governor likes Gwan-sik.

35:38.761 --> 35:39.887
He's very fond of him.

35:42.598 --> 35:44.058
Of course he likes Gwan-sik.

35:45.726 --> 35:47.186
I'm sure he does.

35:47.270 --> 35:50.189
Why?

35:50.273 --> 35:55.069
Why does everyone like Yang Gwan-sik?

35:55.153 --> 35:57.655
GOVERNOR HWANG IN-SU
CONGRATULATIONS ON YOUR INAUGURATION

36:01.617 --> 36:05.121
If your grandmother were here,
she would've thrown a box of red beans.

36:22.805 --> 36:24.223
What the hell are you doing?

36:24.307 --> 36:25.266
Hey!

36:26.058 --> 36:26.893
Come here!

36:26.976 --> 36:28.060
You fool!

36:28.144 --> 36:30.354
You're so embarrassing.

36:36.110 --> 36:38.905
You gotta stop her.
She's really getting out of hand.

36:43.201 --> 36:46.204
Man, she really loves Busan.

36:46.287 --> 36:48.623
She always calls herself Literary Girl.

36:48.706 --> 36:51.500
You're no bookworm! You're just a worm!

36:59.383 --> 37:01.093
Look, she's dancing with the pole.

37:01.177 --> 37:03.930
Throw red beans at her! Throw them!

37:11.771 --> 37:12.605
Father!

37:13.231 --> 37:15.608
Let her be. Let her have her fun.

37:17.151 --> 37:19.779
It's a good thing I started raising you.

37:19.862 --> 37:21.906
Let's go, my good boy.

37:22.782 --> 37:24.242
Where's Goldie?

37:24.325 --> 37:25.743
Come on, my Goldie.

37:25.826 --> 37:30.414
Oh dear, let's go home, my good boy.

37:42.134 --> 37:42.969
Father.

37:44.053 --> 37:44.887
I'll carry her.

37:45.471 --> 37:46.597
Are you that happy?

37:48.057 --> 37:48.891
Yeah.

37:49.642 --> 37:50.476
I'm happy.

37:51.811 --> 37:54.730
I'm so happy.

37:56.315 --> 37:59.694
You're not a runner-up, a vice president,
or a deputy chief anymore.

38:00.444 --> 38:01.904
You really are a chief.

38:04.407 --> 38:05.449
But you know,

38:06.534 --> 38:10.288
I finally got rid of the "deputy"
in my title after 30 years,

38:12.206 --> 38:15.042
but the person I want to tell the most
isn't here.

38:20.548 --> 38:25.011
My childhood was so difficult
that I never missed it.

38:26.929 --> 38:29.181
But if I was asked to go back…

38:31.892 --> 38:33.519
I'd do it all over again.

38:35.187 --> 38:36.397
Just so I could hold

38:37.148 --> 38:39.233
my mom's hand again.

38:40.401 --> 38:43.654
Actually, the reason
I'm the vice president and a runner-up now

38:44.238 --> 38:46.615
is because I wanna be the chief one day.

38:47.116 --> 38:48.284
Even with diving,

38:48.367 --> 38:51.203
you start in shallow waters
before moving to deeper ones.

38:52.747 --> 38:55.708
I'll gain experience little by little
and become a chief one day.

38:55.791 --> 38:58.336
No one can beat a chief.

38:59.545 --> 39:02.590
Even Auntie Gyeong-ja
repays her loans to the chief.

39:03.090 --> 39:06.719
Okay, you be the chief one day
so I can be the chief's mother.

39:07.803 --> 39:09.972
Prepare enough rice cakes that day.

39:10.473 --> 39:14.268
I'm going to make so many rice cakes
that they'll pile up like that mountain.

39:14.352 --> 39:16.812
-Because you'd be happy?
-Yes, I'd be happy.

39:17.313 --> 39:18.314
I'd be happy too.

39:20.608 --> 39:21.734
I'm holding back

39:22.401 --> 39:25.071
because I want to express
my happiness that day.

39:28.449 --> 39:30.368
I'm not going to hold back.

39:30.951 --> 39:33.579
Every time I'm really happy,
I'll let everyone know.

39:33.662 --> 39:34.497
Why hold back?

39:37.500 --> 39:40.461
Aunties, make sure
you take double portions, all right?

39:42.546 --> 39:43.422
Goodness me.

39:45.132 --> 39:48.302
You all fed and raised me
with these red-ribboned nets.

39:48.386 --> 39:51.263
Now go around and brag about me
on my mom's behalf.

39:51.347 --> 39:53.432
Honestly.

39:53.516 --> 39:55.643
You must've used a ton of rice.

39:55.726 --> 39:57.561
Why did you make so many rice cakes?

39:58.354 --> 40:01.649
Apparently, this is from our Gwang-rye!

40:02.525 --> 40:03.526
Oh dear.

40:04.360 --> 40:05.361
Gwang-rye!

40:06.028 --> 40:09.615
Your daughter is all grown up.
She's the chief now.

40:11.325 --> 40:15.287
She was only ten when she sat
on this very floor in mourning clothes.

40:15.371 --> 40:20.209
Back then,
I wondered whether she'd make it.

40:20.918 --> 40:24.088
Who knew she would not only survive
but also thrive?

40:24.171 --> 40:25.714
If Gwang-rye were still with us,

40:25.798 --> 40:29.885
she would have taken a drum
and played it all around Hallasan.

40:29.969 --> 40:33.180
You dug into the frozen ground
with your tiny hands

40:33.264 --> 40:34.974
and buried your heart in it.

40:35.057 --> 40:37.268
This must be your harvest season at last.

40:39.311 --> 40:43.983
Gwang-rye's persimmon tree is fruitful.
So fruitful!

40:45.025 --> 40:46.152
Indeed,

40:46.235 --> 40:48.320
it was fall, the season of harvest,

40:49.113 --> 40:52.783
when all kinds of fruits were ripening.

41:05.796 --> 41:09.633
Each one filled
with its own chaotic story.

41:11.844 --> 41:15.181
Each one growing
under its own ray of sunlight.

41:24.732 --> 41:25.566
Hey, look.

41:34.867 --> 41:35.701
Why?

41:36.452 --> 41:37.453
Sorry?

41:37.536 --> 41:39.371
Why are you in the front seat again?

41:41.790 --> 41:42.625
Just because

41:44.335 --> 41:45.294
it's fun.

41:48.589 --> 41:49.840
It really annoys her

41:51.467 --> 41:53.260
when I do that.

41:53.344 --> 41:55.054
That mean girl you told me about?

41:55.137 --> 41:55.971
Yes.

41:56.055 --> 41:56.889
Yeong-beom!

42:02.645 --> 42:03.479
Yeong-beom.

42:16.492 --> 42:18.410
Jjajangmyeon was all you wanted?

42:20.287 --> 42:21.914
So you don't know that car either?

42:21.997 --> 42:24.833
There's something really weird
about Yang Geum-myeong, right?

42:25.334 --> 42:26.710
Stop saying weird things.

42:27.711 --> 42:29.630
Not all poor people lack class.

42:29.713 --> 42:32.216
Ye-rim, stop taking her side.

42:32.299 --> 42:35.761
She's always mean to you,
so why are you always so nice to her?

42:36.345 --> 42:39.431
It's because her mind is twisted.
I can understand her.

42:39.515 --> 42:41.100
What do you mean she's twisted?

42:42.393 --> 42:45.563
My dad and I had a little talk
about Geum-myeong.

42:45.646 --> 42:48.983
He said those who rise from nothing
often get twisted.

42:49.066 --> 42:51.652
She must've been the best
in her tiny town.

42:51.735 --> 42:54.655
But it's different here,
so her mind must be twisted.

42:56.198 --> 42:58.450
She feels more inferior every day.

42:58.534 --> 43:00.703
Dad says the better person
should let it go.

43:01.203 --> 43:02.454
That's what class is.

43:02.538 --> 43:03.372
But…

43:05.457 --> 43:07.042
why would she be like that?

43:08.002 --> 43:09.461
Her GPA is higher than yours.

43:09.545 --> 43:11.547
By 0.2. Just a 0.2 difference.

43:11.630 --> 43:13.048
-She's taller too.
-By 2 cm?

43:13.132 --> 43:14.133
And…

43:15.551 --> 43:17.886
You must remember everything about her.

43:19.096 --> 43:20.889
-What else?
-Anyway…

43:20.973 --> 43:22.433
Don't "anyway" me. What else?

43:23.642 --> 43:27.396
Anyway, Geum-myeong was
the first chosen to go to Japan.

43:27.896 --> 43:31.191
If she hadn't given it up,
you wouldn't be going, but thanks to her--

43:31.275 --> 43:33.611
If I were a professor,
I would have chosen her too.

43:34.236 --> 43:36.113
My family can afford to send me abroad.

43:36.196 --> 43:39.617
Naturally, the school would support
a less fortunate girl.

43:39.700 --> 43:40.534
Ye-rim.

43:40.618 --> 43:42.620
Geum-myeong's family is doing well.

43:42.703 --> 43:44.872
-Her father's a boat captain.
-He's a fisherman.

43:44.955 --> 43:46.582
Birds of a feather flock together!

43:48.667 --> 43:49.668
You sure are classy.

43:52.546 --> 43:53.422
I'm not gonna eat.

43:58.093 --> 43:59.762
She dumped you, didn't she?

43:59.845 --> 44:02.264
What's with that foreign car? Tell me!

44:03.349 --> 44:05.184
You're just dying to know, aren't you?

44:05.267 --> 44:08.771
PRIVATE TUTORING BAN SPARKS ODDITIES
TUTORING EVEN TAKING PLACE IN MOVING CARS!

44:13.859 --> 44:15.694
23RD TYPHOON "PHYLLIS"
CAUTIONS IN FISHING TOWNS

44:15.778 --> 44:17.154
Will the waves be safe today?

44:18.155 --> 44:23.243
Regardless of whether the waves are safe,
my dad still takes his boat out.

44:24.953 --> 44:27.539
I'm the only one
who always worries about him.

44:27.623 --> 44:30.000
-I'll see you guys.
-Bye.

44:40.219 --> 44:41.053
Okay, let's go!

44:41.136 --> 44:43.639
Speak with respect!

44:44.431 --> 44:48.185
"Shut the fuck"? Jesus Christ.

44:48.268 --> 44:51.897
You can't even spell "Wednesday."
Where'd you learn to curse?

44:55.693 --> 44:57.569
Jenny, can you spell "Wednesday" now?

44:57.653 --> 45:00.030
-Write it down here. Now.
-Don't.

45:02.074 --> 45:04.410
Why is your name even Oh Jenny?

45:04.493 --> 45:06.662
I was scared you were from overseas.

45:07.454 --> 45:09.415
Anyone else would've been fired by now.

45:09.498 --> 45:10.874
Not just fired but--

45:10.958 --> 45:12.501
Just fire me already.

45:13.419 --> 45:17.506
Actually, why don't you fire me?
I heard no other tutor lasted a month.

45:17.589 --> 45:19.216
Well, look forward to it.

45:20.342 --> 45:21.719
Put your feet down!

45:22.761 --> 45:24.388
Seriously!

45:33.981 --> 45:36.984
Hey, Oh Jammy. You didn't memorize
the vocabulary, did you?

45:38.110 --> 45:39.862
You just come here to eat, don't you?

45:41.405 --> 45:44.491
I think your housekeeper can cook dishes
from all over the country.

45:44.575 --> 45:46.785
She said these glass noodles
are from Busan.

45:47.286 --> 45:50.122
That lady always uses
other people's money to gain favor.

45:51.540 --> 45:54.626
You're such a brat
that she might quit here soon too.

45:55.711 --> 45:58.505
She's been here the longest.
Mom keeps her for some reason.

46:00.215 --> 46:04.219
People don't stay at your house
for very long, do they?

46:05.137 --> 46:05.971
Why?

46:07.973 --> 46:09.057
Come on, why?

46:12.019 --> 46:12.853
Well,

46:14.563 --> 46:18.400
why haven't I ever met
your mother and father?

46:18.484 --> 46:20.319
But that's better, isn't it?

46:20.402 --> 46:23.113
Well, I'd like to see their faces
at least once.

46:23.197 --> 46:24.990
Mom saw you. Just not at home.

46:26.116 --> 46:27.451
Your mom saw me?

46:27.534 --> 46:28.577
Where?

46:28.660 --> 46:30.454
You had your picture on your résumé.

46:31.038 --> 46:32.372
Just fill the time and go.

46:32.456 --> 46:35.459
Honestly, you're here for the jar,
not 'cause you like me.

46:36.084 --> 46:37.544
For you, it's love-hate.

46:38.128 --> 46:39.546
For the jar, it's pure love.

46:40.047 --> 46:43.967
Can you do something about your bangs
and how you part your hair?

46:44.051 --> 46:46.345
You don't look like you're from Seoul!

46:46.428 --> 46:49.097
Why are you so interested in my hairstyle?

46:50.307 --> 46:53.018
I mean, do you and I really look alike?

46:53.101 --> 46:53.936
What?

46:55.312 --> 46:57.147
I'm the sexier one, right?

46:57.231 --> 46:59.650
"Sexy"? Did you just say sexy?

47:01.026 --> 47:01.985
Hey!

47:02.069 --> 47:03.987
Spell "sexy" right here. Spell it.

47:04.071 --> 47:06.532
I can spell that one. S-E--

47:06.615 --> 47:07.449
Stop it.

47:09.535 --> 47:11.078
-S-E!
-Stop it!

47:11.161 --> 47:12.871
Is that all you're interested in?

47:12.955 --> 47:14.998
How dare you. Seriously.

47:25.759 --> 47:28.387
Mom said take what you earned.
No more, no less.

47:30.848 --> 47:36.728
Your mother always puts me
to the test every single time.

47:47.698 --> 47:50.200
Hello? Yeah, what?

47:50.284 --> 47:51.827
Just grab a handful.

47:51.910 --> 47:53.579
Charge double for a dumb student.

47:55.122 --> 47:56.164
What is it?

47:59.126 --> 48:01.086
My mom's coming up. She wants to see you.

48:01.753 --> 48:03.881
-What? Right now?
-Just go.

48:06.508 --> 48:07.509
I said just go.

48:33.076 --> 48:34.244
Ms. Yang.

48:34.328 --> 48:36.455
That's real white porcelain.

48:40.459 --> 48:42.419
I have everything now.

48:42.502 --> 48:45.047
I even have white porcelain
and blue porcelain at home.

48:45.756 --> 48:48.759
The one thing we don't have
is a good education.

48:50.802 --> 48:51.803
I see.

48:51.887 --> 48:54.556
I deeply regret
the limited education I had.

48:54.640 --> 48:56.600
I wanted to live vicariously
through my child,

48:56.683 --> 48:59.186
but sadly, she inherited my intellect.

49:02.439 --> 49:05.525
We'll improve her grades gradually.

49:06.443 --> 49:09.154
We can't afford to wait
for them to improve gradually.

49:09.237 --> 49:11.448
Life doesn't wait for anyone, does it?

49:12.699 --> 49:13.533
I see.

49:14.034 --> 49:17.245
Are you saying I should stop coming…

49:17.329 --> 49:19.873
Jenny is rich,
but she doesn't have the brains.

49:19.957 --> 49:22.626
You earned your way through school,
but you're smart.

49:22.709 --> 49:24.670
I'm saying we should share what we have.

49:26.004 --> 49:29.341
I'll give you an ace

49:29.424 --> 49:31.802
so you can hit a blackjack.

49:32.427 --> 49:35.931
It took us two years to find a tutor
who looked like Jenny.

49:36.014 --> 49:37.641
I won't beat around the bush.

49:38.433 --> 49:39.267
Ms. Yang.

49:40.435 --> 49:42.312
Please take her college entrance exam.

50:01.248 --> 50:03.709
STUDENT ID
OH JENNY

50:05.043 --> 50:07.838
If she gets into
one of the top three universities,

50:07.921 --> 50:10.298
I'll buy you
a three-bed apartment in Seoul.

50:10.382 --> 50:12.843
For anything less, a two-bed instead.

50:20.976 --> 50:23.145
NOTICE
LIST OF APPROVED APPLICANTS FOR DORMS

50:25.188 --> 50:28.108
If a name isn't on the list,
can't they live in the dorms?

50:28.817 --> 50:29.776
No.

50:32.487 --> 50:33.947
I wonder how much the rent is

50:35.323 --> 50:36.575
for boarding houses here.

50:38.618 --> 50:39.703
It's expensive.

50:40.662 --> 50:41.830
It'll be expensive.

51:08.648 --> 51:11.318
Is he picking a fight or what?

51:12.152 --> 51:15.822
The day of this historic election,
December 16th, is upon us,

51:15.906 --> 51:18.325
with the eyes of the world closely on us.

51:18.825 --> 51:21.787
It's been 16 years
since we last voted freely for president.

51:21.870 --> 51:24.122
The atmosphere was solemn and serious.

51:25.707 --> 51:28.251
They say dorm assignments
are drawn at random,

51:28.335 --> 51:30.253
but I think something is fishy.

51:30.837 --> 51:34.800
Apparently, South Korea is one
of the most corrupt countries.

51:36.468 --> 51:39.096
So, who are you voting for?

51:41.181 --> 51:43.850
I think we need to call
the military police to take him.

51:43.934 --> 51:46.603
-What?
-Why is a soldier near the girls' dorm?

51:47.979 --> 51:49.689
The guys' dorms are nearby.

51:50.440 --> 51:53.193
They come and go while on their leave.

51:55.862 --> 51:57.114
Who did you vote for?

51:59.908 --> 52:01.868
Can we get him locked up in the brig?

52:08.667 --> 52:10.168
One, two, three.

52:17.092 --> 52:18.218
Hello, Father!

52:24.224 --> 52:27.060
Well, we met once
at the admission ceremony.

52:27.644 --> 52:31.064
My name is Park Yeong-beom.
I'm a friend of Geum-myeong.

52:36.987 --> 52:41.658
I also took a few pictures
of your family that day, and…

52:45.453 --> 52:49.875
So, you must have taken a plane
and then a bus to see Geum-myeong.

52:51.418 --> 52:52.377
So why?

52:53.336 --> 52:55.130
-Sir?
-Why would you call me "Father"?

52:56.506 --> 52:58.216
-Sorry?
-You said, "Hello, Father."

52:58.300 --> 53:00.594
Why did you call me "Father"?
For what reason?

53:00.677 --> 53:02.012
TEST IDENTIFICATION SLIP
OH JENNY

53:02.095 --> 53:02.929
Dear me.

53:04.472 --> 53:05.307
Oh dear.

53:06.141 --> 53:09.769
Ma'am, we could get into
serious trouble doing this.

53:09.853 --> 53:13.857
Tutoring is already illegal,
so my heart races every time I come here.

53:15.066 --> 53:18.028
Your heart needs to race
to make some money.

53:18.528 --> 53:20.822
There's no jackpot
if you don't bet on anything.

53:20.906 --> 53:22.949
If I got caught, I'd be expelled.

53:23.033 --> 53:27.871
Exactly, the high risk of expulsion
is why you'd get an apartment.

53:29.789 --> 53:34.336
The exam isn't a joke.
How could I ever be Jenny?

53:35.045 --> 53:38.840
Whoever the proctor is,
I will offer them a bribe.

53:38.924 --> 53:44.054
I'll have everything set up perfectly
so you won't have to worry about a thing.

53:46.014 --> 53:50.602
You earn money
by doing what you're good at.

53:50.685 --> 53:53.146
I'll support you
by doing what I'm good at.

53:53.230 --> 53:55.273
Isn't it fair, proper, and profitable

53:55.357 --> 53:57.525
to earn a living
by doing what you're good at?

53:58.526 --> 54:01.905
Just take the plunge this once
and grab the ace.

54:04.950 --> 54:06.243
Ma'am, the thing is--

54:06.326 --> 54:07.160
No.

54:08.036 --> 54:09.746
I don't want your answer now.

54:10.413 --> 54:11.539
Think carefully.

54:11.623 --> 54:14.251
Think very carefully before you speak.

54:20.298 --> 54:24.427
You didn't get a scholarship,
and you have to leave the dorms, right?

54:24.511 --> 54:26.429
Are you really giving up
on studying abroad?

54:26.513 --> 54:29.307
How do you know all that?

54:29.391 --> 54:31.101
Like I said, think carefully.

54:32.060 --> 54:33.979
Don't just think about yourself.

54:34.062 --> 54:37.023
Think of your parents
who work so hard for you.

54:37.107 --> 54:40.360
For a dragon to really rise from a stream,

54:41.069 --> 54:44.114
the stream has to dry up, right?

54:46.658 --> 54:47.659
Come with me.

54:48.868 --> 54:50.620
Hey! Go to your room.

54:57.127 --> 54:58.086
Young lady!

54:59.045 --> 55:01.089
Young lady! Wait up!

55:02.007 --> 55:02.924
Goodness me.

55:03.842 --> 55:05.677
Did you come out of unit 908?

55:06.303 --> 55:08.346
Sorry? Why did you…

55:08.430 --> 55:09.556
If you run,

55:10.056 --> 55:12.100
I can't catch up with you.

55:12.684 --> 55:14.185
Why would I run?

55:14.269 --> 55:15.895
You stole something from there, no?

55:16.521 --> 55:17.355
Sorry?

55:18.231 --> 55:21.484
Just give it here.
Let's not make this any worse.

55:25.655 --> 55:27.115
Is that what that lady said?

55:28.908 --> 55:31.536
I don't want to hear your answer now.

55:32.329 --> 55:33.830
Just take these with you.

55:35.415 --> 55:37.667
Look at them two or three times
or even more.

55:37.751 --> 55:38.835
Then we'll talk again.

55:39.794 --> 55:44.758
Frankly, trying to rise as a dragon
from a stream is selfish, you know?

55:45.592 --> 55:48.553
You'd think the dragon
would give back to its parents,

55:48.636 --> 55:50.138
but just think about it.

55:50.221 --> 55:53.558
Your father is still on that boat
because of you.

55:54.267 --> 55:56.853
And he'll stay on that boat
for the rest of his life.

56:00.482 --> 56:04.861
My father also trusted his eldest son,
who said he'd take the bar exam,

56:04.944 --> 56:08.031
and he fed his cows until the day he died.

56:10.075 --> 56:14.579
If I think of my mom and dad,
there's nothing more for me to ponder.

56:14.662 --> 56:17.916
It'd be great for me to earn an apartment
by doing what I'm good at.

56:18.416 --> 56:20.543
Yes. I like that you're so frank.

56:20.627 --> 56:22.837
But thinking of my mom and dad,
I can't do it.

56:23.546 --> 56:24.381
What?

56:24.464 --> 56:27.717
I was taught to be the last in my class
rather than cheat.

56:28.385 --> 56:32.013
I was taught not to even pick up
a ten-won coin at the playground.

56:32.097 --> 56:35.892
My mom and dad would never approve
of me living life shamelessly.

56:37.310 --> 56:39.104
Are you trying to tell me something?

56:39.187 --> 56:40.230
Also,

56:40.730 --> 56:43.858
if I take the test for Jenny
and she happens to get accepted,

56:43.942 --> 56:45.819
another girl like me won't make it.

56:46.861 --> 56:49.447
I can't bear the thought
of a girl like me not making it

56:50.407 --> 56:51.991
because of a fraud.

56:52.700 --> 56:54.452
She'd die of heartbreak.

56:55.161 --> 56:56.746
Ms. Yang Geum-myeong.

56:57.414 --> 57:01.668
When you have resources and act nobly,
you are seen as a person of integrity.

57:01.751 --> 57:05.004
But when a poor girl pretends to be noble,
it's deemed reckless courage.

57:05.088 --> 57:09.551
Sending a girl who can't spell "Wednesday"
to a top-three school would be reckless--

57:09.634 --> 57:11.177
-Reckless courage.
-Hey!

57:12.554 --> 57:16.349
Let Jenny find her path
by doing what she's good at.

57:17.142 --> 57:19.769
Isn't that fair, proper,
and profitable for Jenny?

57:20.728 --> 57:22.188
Yeah, I want to be a singer.

57:27.485 --> 57:28.570
I'll be going now.

57:30.113 --> 57:33.700
This is why I hate
people who rise from nothing.

57:33.783 --> 57:39.372
You have absolutely nothing,
yet pride is all you have to show off!

57:41.583 --> 57:43.460
Dumb and rude, so it should be quadruple.

57:46.796 --> 57:48.548
I'll take my extra pay, then.

58:06.232 --> 58:07.734
I'm not a thief.

58:07.817 --> 58:10.612
I know. It's not fear
that makes people avoid her.

58:10.695 --> 58:13.364
It’s my money,
but I'll give it up just to avoid them.

58:16.701 --> 58:17.535
And the ring?

58:18.286 --> 58:19.120
Sorry?

58:19.204 --> 58:21.456
Diamond. The diamond ring.

58:35.970 --> 58:38.389
They wished every day

58:38.890 --> 58:42.769
that the world beyond their embrace
would always be gentle.

58:43.269 --> 58:44.437
Ma'am!

58:46.356 --> 58:47.482
Ma'am!

58:48.608 --> 58:50.235
Hey! Oh Jammy!

58:50.318 --> 58:52.278
Hey, open the door!

58:54.447 --> 58:59.202
Hey! Why am I a thief? Why?

58:59.786 --> 59:01.871
But the world away from their embrace

59:03.373 --> 59:04.374
was a jungle.

01:01:51.541 --> 01:01:55.962
"IN THE HOPE THAT OUR ECHOES
WILL FLOW AND FLOW, UNTIL THEY REACH YOU."

01:02:02.927 --> 01:02:05.346
Subtitle translation by: Sung In Jang
